spec mg06-merge-on-match-vs-update: 2 sessions, 6 permutations
# MG06. s1 updates n.v; s2 runs MERGE (n:K {k:'a'}) ON MATCH SET n.v = 2 with an
# older snapshot. The MERGE matches at its snapshot, and its ON MATCH SET is a write
# to a node whose head is not visible to it: refused (F2). PostgreSQL's
# insert-conflict-do-update-3 updates a tuple its snapshot cannot see; GoGraph must
# never do that.

starting permutation: s1w s1c s2m s2c
step s1w: MATCH (n:K {k:'a'}) SET n.v = 1 RETURN n.v AS v
v
-
1
(1 row)
step s1c: COMMIT
step s2m: MERGE (n:K {k:'a'}) ON MATCH SET n.v = 2 RETURN n.v AS v
ERROR: serialization conflict
step s2c: COMMIT
ERROR: cypher: transaction poisoned by a prior failed Exec statement — call Rollback
final final: MATCH (n:K) RETURN n.k AS k, n.v AS v ORDER BY k, v
k  |v
---+-
